README


command: ‘connect CTS’

starts 
1) data logging and sensor display window
2) system status message window
3) keep interactive command interface in terminal window



launcher script ('connect') is located in:

/usr/local/bin/connect

# --- Configuration ---
LOGGER_SCRIPT="/home/lsu-neutrino/Desktop/CTS/serial_logger.py"
PLOTTER_SCRIPT="/home/lsu-neutrino/Desktop/CTS/realtime_plotter.py"
PIPE_PATH="/home/lsu-neutrino/Desktop/CTS/logs/arduino_input.pipe"
PLOTTER_ERR_LOG="/home/lsu-neutrino/Desktop/CTS/logs/plotter_errors.log"
# ---------------------


Other Setup NOTES:

1. Install Dependencies
 You need the pyserial library to talk to the Arduino. Open your terminal and run:
 "pip install pyserial"

2. The Python Script:
The script is: serial_logger.py.
Make sure to update your serial port (usually /dev/ttyACM0 or /dev/ttyUSB0) and matching baud rate as needed.

Default settings:
# --- Configuration ---
SERIAL_PORT = "/dev/ttyACM0"  # Adjust to your port
BAUD_RATE = 115200  # Adjust to match Arduino Serial.begin()
LOG_DIR = "./logs"  # Directory to store logs

3. Environment setup requirements:
a) Add /home/$USER/.local/bin to your PATH requires you to update your shell configuration file. This ensures the change remains active every time you open a new terminal.

e.g. for Bash (/bin/bash):
"echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.bashrc"

b) Apply the Changes:
    To make the changes take effect immediately in your current terminal window without logging out, run: "source ~/.bashrc"   [If using bash]


---------
for debugging it may be useful to run the serial logger by itself:

i) Run the Script
Navigate to the directory where you saved serial_logger.py and execute it using Python 3:
"python3 serial_logger.py"

ii) How to Monitor and Stop it:
To view the data live: Open a second terminal window, navigate to the same folder, and watch the logs generate in real-time using:
"tail -f logs/CTS_Arduino_log_*.csv"

To stop the logger: Go back to your main terminal window running the Python script and press Ctrl + C. It will safely close the active log file and release the serial port.
